DESIGN.md
PRODUCT.md

.impeccable

# Secrets. Each service keeps its own .gitignore, but the rule goes here too,
# because a pattern in one directory does not cover another and `.env.production`
# is a file anyone might add without thinking about it. Values never belong in
# the repository — backend/.env.example documents the shape of the file and
# carries none. The negation below is what keeps that example file committable.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.keyword-qa
.claude
.feed-qa
